<div class="content prose">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="content__intro">Math Direct collects nothing about you. There are no accounts, no tracking, and no cookies.</p>

  <h2>No accounts</h2>
  <p>You do not create an account or give an email address. Every part of the app works without identifying yourself.</p>

  <h2>No tracking</h2>
  <p>The app uses no analytics and no third-party scripts. Nothing you do is monitored or recorded by anyone.</p>

  <h2>What your browser keeps</h2>
  <p>The app keeps its records in your browser's storage, on your device. They never leave it. They are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Each child's name, as you typed it</li>
    <li>Lessons finished, with the firm answers and errors each time a lesson was taught</li>
    <li>Mastery test and placement test results</li>
    <li>The last few results for each addition and subtraction fact</li>
    <li>Notes you write</li>
    <li>Whether you dismissed the Install card</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can erase them on the <a href="/records/">Records</a> screen or by clearing the browser's data for this site.</p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>The whole program is on <a href="https://github.com/jonajinga/math-direct">GitHub</a>, so anyone can check these statements.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ meta.email }}">{{ meta.email }}</a>.</p>
</div>
